# VMap Studio

A modular, cross-platform (Linux · Windows · macOS) mind-mapping and visual-thinking
desktop application written in **Python 3.11+** and **PySide6 / Qt 6**.

> **Status: Phase 1 of 10 (foundation).** This build is a working mind-map editor with a
> native file format. Features that are not implemented are hidden from the UI, and the
> CLI says "not implemented yet" for planned commands. See [ROADMAP.md](ROADMAP.md) and
> [FEATURE_MATRIX.md](FEATURE_MATRIX.md) for the exact state.
> The only supported file format so far is the native `.vmap` format. XMind, FreeMind and
> other formats are planned (Phase 4–5) and are **not** claimed to work yet.

## Quick start

```bash
python -m venv .venv
source .venv/bin/activate          # Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -e ".[dev]"
vmap-studio                        # or: python -m vmap   (optionally followed by a .vmap path)
```

Without installing: `pip install PySide6` and then `python -m vmap` from the project folder.

## What works in Phase 1

- Main window with menus, toolbar, Properties panel, Overview navigator, sheet tabs and status bar
- Topics: add child/sibling/parent, in-place multi-line editing, delete, multi-select, box select
- Drag and drop topics to re-parent or reorder, keyboard navigation, fold/unfold, sort
- Copy/cut/paste/duplicate, including pasting an indented plain-text outline
- Three structures: balanced mind map, logic chart (right), left map
- Theme engine (versioned JSON) with four built-in themes, import/export and per-topic style overrides
- Notes per topic, find & replace (case, whole word, regex, notes)
- Unlimited (or configurable) undo/redo; every operation, including Replace All, is one step
- Native `.vmap` open/save (atomic writes, hardened parser, conversion reports), PNG/SVG export
- Zen Mode, full screen, grid, zoom/pan (wheel, pinch, middle mouse), recent files
- Right-to-left text (Persian, Arabic, Hebrew) inside topics; every UI string goes through `tr()`

## Keyboard essentials

| Action | Keys |
|---|---|
| New subtopic | `Tab` / `Insert` |
| New sibling after / before | `Enter` / `Shift+Enter` |
| New parent topic | `Ctrl/⌘+Enter` |
| Edit topic | `F2`, `Space`, or start typing |
| Delete | `Delete` / `Backspace` |
| Move topic up / down | `Alt+↑` / `Alt+↓` |
| Fold / unfold | `Ctrl/⌘+/` |
| Find / Replace | `Ctrl/⌘+F` / `Ctrl+H` |
| Zen Mode | `Ctrl/⌘+Shift+M` (`Esc` to leave) |

The full list is in **Help → Keyboard Shortcuts**.

## Command line

```bash
vmap new demo.vmap --title "Kubernetes" --theme rainbow
vmap validate demo.vmap
vmap info demo.vmap --json
vmap theme list
vmap open demo.vmap
```

## Data locations

Settings (SQLite), user themes and rotating logs live in the platform's application-data
folder; **Help → Diagnostics** shows the exact path. Set `VMAP_DATA_DIR` to use another
folder (for example, a portable installation). Documents are never stored in the database.

## Tests

```bash
pip install -e ".[dev]"
pytest                             # GUI tests run headless (QT_QPA_PLATFORM=offscreen)
```

